"Johhny" <exter_c@hotmail.com> writes:

> If your doing integer intensive work you will most likely find a
> difference with the increased cache. If you dont do integer intensive
> work you probably wont notice any major difference. Although there are
> some X apps that will perform slightly better with cache (from what Ive
> heard).

Integer vs. floating point is not the issue.  All that matters is
memory access patterns.  Cache helps if your program does frequent
accesses to a data set that fits entirely in the cache.  As soon as
the working set gets larger than the cache, a lot of the speed
increase vanishes.

