Let's set aside that very kind offer for a moment.

My first problem is that although I can build 2.4.29 SMP, it still bombs 
out and I don't know why.  Come to think of it, I don't really know 
where to start looking.

As my most immediate need is to get access to the big new disk, I'm now 
trying a single processor build of 2.4.29, so I'll see how I get on with 
that, i.e. will it boot, will it access the disk with the generic ATA 
drivers.


The odd thing is that as it compiles, I can see the switches to gcc 
include -mcpu=ev4 and -mev6.

Man gcc doesn't explicitly describe -mev6, but it does say

     "-m68040  Generate  output  for a 68040.  This is the default
     when the compiler  is  configured  for  68040-based systems."

Man gcc doesn't refer to -mcpu=cpu-type for the Alpha, but re MIPS, it 
also says:

     "-mcpu=cpu-type
               Assume  the  defaults for the machine type cpu-type
               when scheduling instructions.  The default cpu-type
               is  default,  which  picks the longest cycles times
               for any of the machines, in order that the code run
               at  reasonable  rates  on  all  MIPS  cpu's.  Other
               choices for cpu-type are r2000, r3000,  r4000,  and
               r6000.   While  picking  a  specific  cpu-type will
               schedule things appropriately for  that  particular
               chip,  the compiler will not generate any code that
               does not meet level 1 of the MIPS ISA  (instruction
               set  architecture)  without  the  -mips2  or -mips3
               switches being used."

so by extrapolation, I'd assume that this would generate code for EV6, 
but schedule instructions for EV4.

The installed CPUs are all EV4s, so why is it compiling for anything 
other than that ?  I don't see where I can configure the particular CPU 
it generates code for, but will generating instructions for EV6 result 
in incompatible code being produced, or just in some loss of 
optimisation ?

Maybe this is the root cause of my problem ?  .config says the CPU is 
EV4, so where might the EV6 reference be coming from ?


Cheers, J/.
